// The port of connect_within() must be an integer, and an integer is an Int or
// an integer-valued Number (spec/05-stdlib.md, Integer arguments). The Int
// form is the one a program computes, and the limit stays a Number: a
// fractional port is a runtime error that halts the program, checked before
// the limit and before any connection attempt.
// COVERS: integer-arg connect-within-port
// STATUS: error
// TIMEOUT: 10
// CHECK: connected
var l = listen("127.0.0.1", 0);
var c = connect_within("127.0.0.1", int(l.port()), 5);
print "connected";
// The fractional port is the listener's own port plus a half, so an
// implementation that truncates the port connects to the listener and prints
// the next line, and the probe fails. A fixed fractional port such as 1.5
// would only be refused, and a refusal and a fault look the same here: both
// halt with the output above.
connect_within("127.0.0.1", l.port() + 0.5, 5);
print "unreachable";
